/-
# Formations of nilpotent groups of class at most `4` (Kourovka Notebook Problem 10.56)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 10.56 (A. N. Skiba): is the lattice of
formations of finite nilpotent groups of class `≤ 4` distributive?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.PUnit
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coset.Card
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Nilpotent

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentFormationLatticeDistributiveKourovka10Problem56Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 10.56 (A. N.
Skiba). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700671 (`KOU-10.56`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A formation is an isomorphism-closed class of finite groups (in `Type`) that contains the trivial
group and is closed under quotients and subdirect products. The lattice consists of the formations
all of whose members are nilpotent of class `≤ 4` (`ζ₄(G) = G`); the meet is the intersection and
the join is the formation generated by the union. Distributivity is the identity `A ∧ (B ∨ C) = (A ∧
B) ∨ (A ∧ C)`.
-/

/-- A class of finite groups, given by its membership predicate. -/
abbrev GroupClass : Type 1 :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], Prop

/-- A formation of finite groups: an isomorphism-closed class of finite groups that contains the
trivial group and is closed under quotients and subdirect products
(`G/N₁, G/N₂ ∈ X → G/(N₁ ∩ N₂) ∈ X`). -/
def IsFormation (X : GroupClass) : Prop :=
  (∀ (G H : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] [Group H] [Finite H], (G ≃* H) → X G → X H) ∧ X Unit ∧
  (∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (N : Subgroup G) [N.Normal], X G → X (G ⧸ N)) ∧
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (N₁ N₂ : Subgroup G) [N₁.Normal] [N₂.Normal],
    X (G ⧸ N₁) → X (G ⧸ N₂) → X (G ⧸ (N₁ ⊓ N₂))

/-- `X` is a formation of finite nilpotent groups of class at most `4`. -/
def IsNilpotentClassFourFormation (X : GroupClass) : Prop :=
  IsFormation X ∧ ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], X G → Subgroup.upperCentralSeries G 4 = ⊤

/-- The intersection (lattice meet) of two classes. -/
def meet (X Y : GroupClass) : GroupClass :=
  fun G _ _ => X G ∧ Y G

/-- The formation generated by `X ∪ Y` (lattice join of formations): the intersection of all
formations containing `X` and `Y`. -/
def formationJoin (X Y : GroupClass) : GroupClass :=
  fun G _ _ => ∀ Z : GroupClass, IsFormation Z → (∀ (H : Type) [Group H] [Finite H], X H → Z H) →
    (∀ (H : Type) [Group H] [Finite H], Y H → Z H) → Z G

/-- Kourovka 10.56 (A. N. Skiba): the lattice of formations of finite nilpotent groups of class at
most `4` is distributive: `A ∧ (B ∨ C) = (A ∧ B) ∨ (A ∧ C)` for all such formations. -/
def nilpotentClassFourFormationsDistributive : Prop :=
  ∀ A B C : GroupClass, IsNilpotentClassFourFormation A → IsNilpotentClassFourFormation B →
    IsNilpotentClassFourFormation C → ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G],
      (A G ∧ formationJoin B C G) ↔ formationJoin (meet A B) (meet A C) G

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 10.56 "No": the lattice of varieties of nilpotent
`2`-groups of class `≤ 4` is not distributive (Belov; Bryce), and `𝔙 ↦ 𝔙 ∩ 𝔉` (`𝔉` the class of
finite groups) embeds it in the lattice of formations (Kovács), with image among the formations of
finite nilpotent groups of class `≤ 4`. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved
Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 10.56 (A. N. Skiba); resolution: Yu. A. Belov, Algebra and Logic 9, no. 6
(1970), 371-374; R. A. Bryce, Philos. Trans. Roy. Soc. London (A) 266 (1970), 281-355, footnote on
p. 335; L. Kovács, letter of 12 May 1988, Kourovka Archive, Problem 10.56 ("No"): the lattice of
varieties of nilpotent 2-groups of class ≤ 4 is non-distributive, and V ↦ V ∩ F embeds it in the
lattice of formations.
-/
public theorem_wanted nilpotentClassFourFormationsDistributive_refuted :
    ¬ nilpotentClassFourFormationsDistributive

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentFormationLatticeDistributiveKourovka10Problem56Wanted
